  "scope": "Launch-day Franklin Assistant progressive-guide successor. Builds on R1306's answer-first follow-up behavior by making the guide stateful within the current page session so it does not ask the same question repeatedly. Each topic now has a two-stage guided path: the first follow-up narrows the resident's situation, and the second moves them toward the next useful action such as permit steps, a local provider, an official source, enrollment, transportation, court/forms, benefits, schedules, contacts or other route-specific help. After two guide prompts on the same topic, Franklin stops prompting unless the user changes topic, reducing intake-form fatigue. Topic changes reset the guide naturally. New chat resets guide state. Profile/provider conversations progress from matching options to website/phone/more-match actions. All guide state remains memory-only for the current page. Grounded OpenAI answers, reading-first scroll, direct-answer-first UX, English/Spanish support, 19,103 profiles, 254 Assistant routes, privacy, safety and no-loss protections remain preserved.",
